Suggests: gnome-shell | plasma-desktop | xfce4 | mate-desktop
Description: parental controls and a master password policy for the desktop
 Sudaeon puts one master password in front of the actions that matter on a
 shared computer: rebooting, shutting down, suspending, logging out, switching
 users, installing software, changing accounts, running sudo in a terminal and
 starting chosen applications.
 .
 The policy is managed from a stock GTK4/libadwaita dashboard with a single
 "Use Sudaeon" master switch and tabs for Power, Enforcement, Users, Schedule,
 Applications, Logs and Advanced settings. Accounts are either Administrators
 (dashboard access, system wide effect), Exempt from Policy or Regular Users.
 .
 Enforcement is implemented with the distribution's own mechanisms - PAM for
 sudo, su and pkexec, polkit rules for graphical administrator prompts, logind
 inhibitors for power and sleep, dconf lockdown keys for the GNOME session and
 desktop-entry overrides for application control - so nothing has to be
 patched and root is never restricted.
 .
 The master password is only ever verified by the setuid helper
 /usr/lib/sudaeon/sudaeon-chkpwd; the dashboard, the CLI and the PAM module
 never see the verifier and the password is never passed in a command line.
 .
 Installing this package does not enforce anything by itself: until the setup
 wizard stores a master password the policy stays switched off.
